<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The app's entitlements for ad-hoc signatures made by Scripts/sign-app.sh (the release dry run). Under the hardened
runtime, library validation refuses the ad-hoc Sparkle.framework in an ad-hoc app ("different Team IDs"), because
neither has a Team ID. Xcode builds get the same exception from RUNTIME_EXCEPTION_DISABLE_LIBRARY_VALIDATION in
Base.xcconfig. A Developer ID build is signed with Zivlet.entitlements instead, and the Developer ID signature gate
(verify-signatures.sh) fails if library validation is off.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
